# Quality

Read `docs/development/TESTING_STRATEGY.md` when adding substantial tests.

- TypeScript strict; avoid unnecessary `any`.
- Favor clear domain functions over abstraction layers with no current value.
- Tests are strongest in `game-core`, selective in session/AI, and minimal for purely visual details.
- No arbitrary coverage target.
- Do not write low-value snapshot/unit tests just to increase test count.
- For UI/game feel, manual testing is first-class and must be included at phase handoff.
- Run focused tests while developing; run the relevant full suite/typecheck/build before phase completion.
- Fix warnings/errors that indicate real defects, but do not derail a phase into unrelated cleanup.
